1
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,320
- Really, girl?
- Yeah, I know.

2
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,480
- Well, how was it?
- Good, how about him?

3
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:21,120
Is he mad?

4
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:24,600
Late again, sweetheart.
What happened? Tell me.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,880
I’m sorry, Santi.
I’m coming from a casting

6
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,800
at Boadilla del Monte
and it was far as fuck.

7
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,840
Why don’t you quit it,
sweetheart?

8
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,960
- You don’t have any luck.
- I’ll have to do something.

9
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:35,200
- What was the casting for?
- A short film.

10
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,840
- Who watches that?
- I do.

11
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:40,360
I watch lots, Santi.
"La olla exprés" was very good.

12
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:42,560
I showed it to you.
Besides this short film was great.

13
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,760
It was from Madrid’s Cinematography
School, a great platform.

14
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:46,640
- You’ve no idea.
- Platform the apron.

15
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,120
Where is it?

16
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:49,840
It’s here.

17
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,640
Put it on already.
I’ll go out.

18
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:53,080
I want the toilets perfectly clean.

19
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:55,640
And please, Belén, prepare
the rolls with spearmint

20
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,040
and lettuce.
It’s not that hard.

21
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,680
- Okay.
- Come on, girls.

22
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,720
You keep watching short films,
I’ll give you a long workday.

23
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,360
I’ll be right back.
Get to work.

24
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:08,120
- Yeah. He’s an asshole.
- Dude, he gets me horny.

25
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,760
Sometimes I imagine
I’m lying here naked with sushi

26
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,960
- all over my body and he fucks me.
- Good for you.

27
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,480
Well, will you get it or not?

28
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,040
I don’t know.
They made me do it thrice.

29
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,360
It’s a beautiful short film
about a young mother

30
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,800
that gets kicked out of home
and has a horrible time.

31
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:25,480
That’s very modern.
It’s like watching the news.

32
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,960
That role is very contemporary.
Why are you crying?

33
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:30,120
I’m not crying.
I’m a little overwhelmed.

34
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,320
- Okay.
- Turn the volume up,

35
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,040
Topacio’s show is about to start.
Olga, it’s on. Come.

36
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:37,240
We’ll talk about
the soldier kids in Syria later.

37
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,960
It’s very interesting, but now
it’s time for Eduardo Casanova.

38
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:44,400
Welcome to "La Galaxia de Topi".
Please, Eduardo, tell me.

39
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:48,200
When you named your debut film
"Cómete una mierda",

40
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:51,240
I guess you had in mind
the current young people situation

41
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,040
and their constant search.

42
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,840
When I started writing
" Cómete una mierda",

43
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,960
producing it and filming it,

44
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,760
my goal was to talk
about eating shit.

45
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,080
- Literally.
- Yeah.

46
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,240
- No background.
- Exactly.

47
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:06,440
You just said it,
it’s literally shit.

48
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:07,520
It’s an incredible moment

49
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,640
because for the first time
in "La galaxia de Topi",

50
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,960
we have a guest nominated
to the next Goya Awards

51
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:16,520
for Best New Actress.
Our favourite girl, Mariona Terés.

52
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:18,480
Mariona, thanks for coming.

53
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,640
You’re much prettier than her.

54
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,240
- She does it really well...
- Much prettier.

55
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,760
Mariona, did you lose weight?

56
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:28,440
Yeah, I lost 7 pounds,
because for Edu’s film

57
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:31,840
I had to gain 22. I had doughnuts
for breakfast and dinner.

58
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:34,960
I wanted her to be chubbier

59
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:38,760
just for the sake of it.
Shit, chubby, everything.

60
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:41,160
- That’s my thing. She’s amazing.
- She does as the director says.

61
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:43,040
She does.
Specially regarding food.

62
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,720
You could be there anytime soon
and I’d watch you from here.

63
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,160
- Stop crying.
- I’m not.

64
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,040
You’re gorgeous and you deserve it.
You’re a very nice girl.

65
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,760
Thanks. Wait, I’ll get it.

66
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,360
"For God’s sake", tell me.

67
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:45,560
Well, Belinda, you’ll have
a wonderful comeback.

68
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,240
Your day will have an incredible
ending filled with joy,

69
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,800
optimism and luck.

70
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,960
Once a year, at PS Management office,

71
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,920
everybody on the team gathers

72
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:56,040
for a tarot card reading
by María Rosa Cobo.

73
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:58,680
See?
The office décor is a bit esoteric.

74
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,840
Miguel Ángel Muñoz
started out with me.

75
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:03,280
I got him his first movie,
"El palomo cojo".

76
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:08,840
And well, Miguel Ángel’s mom
is a fortune teller too.

77
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,280
Cristina Blanco.

78
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,680
She told me
about María Rosa Cobo’s power.

79
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,040
And we’ve been close friends
since 95’.

80
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:18,640
Can you believe it?
21 years.

81
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,920
María Rosa Cobo,
confident and friend.

82
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,880
- Can you tell me about that guy?
- Of course, sweetheart.

83
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,600
For that purpose Belinda,
we’ll ask the cards,

84
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,840
- they’re magic.
- Okay.

85
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:28,960
Are you ready?
Sure?

86
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,800
- For the good and the bad?
- For everything.

87
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,240
These crystals will energize
the cards.

88
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:36,560
Let’s throw this one, too.
A four, good.

89
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,880
A magic number.
Let’s see, darling.

90
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:42,160
- You like him a lot.
- Yeah.

91
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,560
He’s handsome, attractive,
a bit serious...

92
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:48,400
The Fool card,
it means he’s also talkative.

93
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:50,800
- That’s a good feature.
- He makes me laugh.

94
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:51,880
It’s magic.

95
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,040
My God! Belinda, he’s gay.

96
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,040
I knew you would look me like that.

97
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,160
- Are you sure?
- Very.

98
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:03,560
Pretty sure, it’s The Devil’s card.
He really is quite a catch.

99
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,880
- But he’s gay.
- He is.

100
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:08,480
I’m very close to Paca Salas.
I love her a lot.

101
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:15,080
There’s something about her...
It really gets me. It really does.

102
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:18,080
- She knows a lot about magic.
- I know a lot.

103
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:22,600
I wrote a book named
"La magia que hay en ti".

104
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:26,040
Human beings are magic.
To grab a stone is magic.

105
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,320
To live our lives is magic.

106
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:31,240
Humans only have
to work a little harder

107
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:34,560
to get out that power,
that magic within them,

108
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,520
so they can set in motion
their goals.

109
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:42,640
Everybody can have a successful life.

110
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:44,960
You just have to want it.

111
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,880
When there’s a will, there’s a way.
That’s all.

112
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:49,080
- When there’s a will, there’s a way.
- She’s the best.

113
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:51,800
Don’t worry, darling.
You’ve got a bright future.

114
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,480
Really. I promise.

115
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:54,960
Let’s see that future then...

116
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:57,240
"To live and let live,
fairly take and fairly give".

117
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:59,280
- What else?
- My job.

118
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,200
Let’s sprinkle some magic powder.

119
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:04,480
Cut the deck. Let’s see.
Well, he’ll be your friend.

120
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,560
You know, "Who finds a friend,
finds a treasure".

121
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:08,240
Choose one of those.

122
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:09,680
- This one.
- Okay.

123
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:13,080
Well, I loved the cut. I love it.

124
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,400
- Great.
- You’ve got The Sun card.

125
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,280
- Really?
- It means happiness

126
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,280
surrounded by wonderful people.

127
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,640
- Will I do television?
- Not right now.

128
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:24,800
- Really?
- No, theatre, musicals, cabaret...

129
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:27,040
I’ve made a band.
The Washington Band.

130
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,240
Is that so?
Look, The Star card.

131
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:32,880
The star with the sun is the card
of fame and success.

132
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,800
It means you’ll reach the sky,
Belinda.

133
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:38,280
- Great! That’s awesome!
- I’m really happy.

134
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,440
Perfect. Are you sure
about the gay issue?

135
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,360
- Yeah, darling. I’m really sorry.
- Okay.

136
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,680
There are some jobs.
Right now, advertising.

137
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:46,960
- Not that, I told you.
- They’re 6,000 dollars.

138
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,680
When will it be my turn?
I’ve been here for a long time.

139
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,960
Let’s do something
to avoid misunderstandings.

140
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,880
You’ll come in on alphabetical order.

141
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,720
- Antonio Albella is the first.
- I’m letter "R".

142
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:58,400
- Okay, I’m letter "A".
- I’m next, letter "D".

143
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,480
Calm down, everybody.
All of us will get in.

144
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,880
Paca, you must see something
very important about Alex’s cousin.

145
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:05,040
I just want to see my dress
for the Goya Awards,

146
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,400
I got it fixed by a Chinese.
It was horribly tight.

147
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:10,440
- Okay. She’s done now.
- I’ll go first.

148
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:14,160
Please, be quiet or the magic
will fade. All right?

149
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,080
- Girl, you’re gorgeous!
- Yeah, you look pretty.

150
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,880
Stop it! Bye.

151
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,880
Come on, Belinda,
you’ve been here for ages

152
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,680
- and people are waiting outside.
- I’m coming. I’ll take your card.

153
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:27,280
- Well, darling...
- Are you coming to the concert?

154
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,440
- What concert?
- The charity concert.

155
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,080
I told you,
The Washington Band concert.

156
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,200
I can’t. I’ll attend the Goya Awards.

157
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,680
- My girl is nominated.
- Sure, she is.

158
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:37,040
- Good luck.
- Of course.

159
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,480
Anyway, If you can go for a while...

160
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:40,480
Send me your concerts schedule
and I’ll go.

161
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:43,800
I have and you never can.
You’re always busy, Paquita.

162
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:46,240
All right, to the point,

163
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:49,040
- will she win the Goya or not?
- Let’s see. You are very excited.

164
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:50,680
- Of course.
- You are very excited.

165
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:53,800
Mariona is Best New Actress nominee

166
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,800
for "Cómete una mierda"
by Eduardo Casanova.

167
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:58,440
She was also nominated
for The Feroz Award. She won.

168
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:01,880
She lost out The Forqué Award
to another girl. Angy.

169
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:04,280
But well, those awards
are always a mismatch,

170
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,120
so it’s all right.
I’m very excited.

171
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:10,760
It can be a very important moment
for our office. PS.

172
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:16,480
Another Goya after Macarena’s.
Now Mariona’s.

173
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,680
- Will she win the Goya or not?
- Let’s see. All right?

174
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,440
- Okay.
- Let’s see. Cut the deck, darling.

175
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,520
Done...

176
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,240
- Which pile is for me?
- This one.

177
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,880
Good, let’s check the vibes.

178
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,760
- The Sun card, Paquita.
- Really?

179
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,320
The Sun card, darling.
A nice start.

180
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,120
- The Star card.
- God!

181
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,680
- The card of the artists.
- That’s good.

182
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:41,720
The Star means success.
Paquita, it’s the Goya.

183
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,400
- She won the Goya?
- You deserve it.

184
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:46,600
- Oh, my God! I can’t believe it!
- God, I see success,

185
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:48,840
- money, triumph...
- Really?

186
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,400
I promise. The cards don’t lie.

187
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,080
I’ll tell you something.

188
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,440
I dreamed about it
some days ago, you know?

189
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,520
- I had a feeling.
- You’re also a little witch.

190
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:02,240
- High give. I’m happy for you.
- I swear, I can’t believe it.

191
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:05,080
Wait... it’s her, by the way.

192
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:07,040
- We summoned her.
- We did.

193
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:10,120
Let’s listen to her.
She’s doing some pictures.

194
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,680
<i>Paquita, honey, hi</i>.

195
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,320
She doesn’t know
about the Goya yet.

196
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:16,680
<i>I’m going craz</i>y
<i>at the Vogue photo shoot</i>.

197
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,560
<i>You should see me</i>,
<i>I look pretty as fuck</i>.

198
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,480
<i>The way she talks..</i>.

199
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:25,440
<i>I’ll be brief</i>.
<i>How can I say this</i>?

200
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:28,160
<i>Listen, I quit PS</i>.

201
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,280
<i>All right? I wante</i>d
<i>to tell you after the awards</i>,

202
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,960
<i>- but I can’t wait</i>.
- What?

203
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,400
<i>Here, everybody say</i>s
<i>that you’re ancient history</i>,

204
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,280
<i>a bother and I need somebody..</i>.

205
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:42,240
Paquita, let me see the cards.
Look, the Tower card.

206
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,600
Everything crumbles down.

207
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,640
This card doesn’t lie, darling.
She’s leaving.

208
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:53,640
From my experience,
when a relationship ends,

209
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,480
you have to let it go.

210
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:57,360
Because if it doesn’t end,

211
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,480
a new one won’t come.
There are people

212
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,160
who come into this world to meet
three, four or five people.

213
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:05,320
They are life experiences
and you have to let them go.

214
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,240
What am I doing wrong, Magüi?
What is it?

215
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:15,640
Don’t worry, Paca.
Let’s put this away.

216
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,400
We’ll get back to work...

217
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,120
They always leave me.
What am I doing wrong?

218
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,200
I’ll show you Alex’s cousin
videobook.

219
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:25,520
- I’m sure you’ll like it.
- Are you an idiot? Don’t you see?

220
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,360
How can we watch the videobook

221
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,760
of your boyfriend’s cousin?
After all I’ve done

222
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,440
for that ungrateful girl.
All this year, the interviews,

223
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,520
the red carpets, the castings,
everything...

224
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:37,240
She was chosen for Fernando González
Molina’s movie and she quits?

225
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:39,960
What about my 2,000 dollars
Goya dress?

226
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,760
What shall I do?
Wear it and go alone?

227
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,440
I won’t watch any videobook.

228
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,280
I’m going home. For God’s sake!

229
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:50,080
